Report each `receive_messages` turn's own tokens and cost rather than the
session's running totals. The CLI documents `model_usage` and `total_cost_usd` as
cumulative over the session — a resumed session starts them fresh and a
mid-session `/clear` zeroes them — which is the right value for `query()`, where
the session is the invocation, but not for multi-turn mode, where a fresh
`invoke_agent` span opens per turn while the counters keep growing. Turn two
reported turn one's tokens and cost on top of its own, and turn three all three
turns'. The totals are snapshotted when a turn ends and the baseline goes back to
zero on a conversation reset, which is when the CLI's counters do.
